# Force LF on everything that Linux executes.
#
# Git on Windows checks files out as CRLF by default. A shell script or
# entrypoint carrying \r builds fine and then dies at runtime with
#   exec /entry.sh: no such file or directory
# because the \r becomes part of the interpreter path. On this platform that
# surfaces as a healthy build followed by a 502, which is maximally confusing.

* text=auto eol=lf

Dockerfile      text eol=lf
*.dockerfile    text eol=lf
*.sh            text eol=lf
*.bash          text eol=lf
entrypoint*     text eol=lf
docker-entrypoint* text eol=lf
*.yml           text eol=lf
*.yaml          text eol=lf
.deploy         text eol=lf
.env.example    text eol=lf

# Binaries must never be touched.
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.jpeg binary
*.gif binary
*.webp binary
*.ico binary
*.pdf binary
*.woff binary
*.woff2 binary
